To pass credentials in JS code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`, you can follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have installed the package by running `npm install react-native-fbsdk-next`.
2. Next, create a new file called `Credentials.js` and add the following code:
```javascript
import { FacebookAuthProvider } from 'react-native-fbsdk-next';

const credentials = {
  appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID',
  apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY',
};

const authProvider = new FacebookAuthProvider(credentials);

export default authProvider;
```
Replace `YOUR_APP_ID` and `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Facebook app ID and API key.
3. Now, you can import the `authProvider` from the `Credentials.js` file and use it in your other components. For example:
```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, Text, Button } from 'react-native';
import { authProvider } from './Credentials';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const [loggedIn, setLoggedIn] = useState(false);

  const handleLogin = async () => {
    try {
      await authProvider.login();
      setLoggedIn(true);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error logging in:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      <Text>{loggedIn ? 'Logged in' : 'Not logged in'}</Text>
      <Button title="Login" onPress={handleLogin} />
    </View>
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```
This is just a basic example, and you may need to adjust the code to fit your specific requirements. Also, make sure to follow the Facebook Developer documentation for more information on how to use the Facebook SDK for React Native: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/facebook-sdk-for-react-native

